dialogue joined_generic
title: A new face at the fire
trigger: Joined
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  The caravan's newest hero sits apart from the others, near the edge of the firelight, not quite sure of their place yet.
  * You chose us after a long look. That counts for something. -> walked
    if: TrustAtLeast $hero 15
  * You're one of us now. Come closer to the fire. -> signed

node walked hero
  I watched you long enough to know you weren't another collector with a kinder face. That's more than most get from me.
  -> why

node signed hero
  One of you. I've been one of a lot of things. A caravan running from the Choir is new.
  -> why

node why hero
  The others say the old tech wakes when you're near. The orbs we fight with, the Halcyon doors. Is that true?
  -> answer

node answer commander
  The orb at the Commander's belt brightens a little, as if it heard the question.
  * It's true. I don't know why yet. I'd like you to help me find out. -> help
    do: AddTrust $hero 6
  * I came out of the Still. Halcyon's machines remember me, even if I don't. -> still
    do: AddTrust $hero 5
  * It's true, and it's why you're safer with me than without me. -> safer
    do: AddTrust $hero -2

node help hero
  Help. Not follow. Nobody's asked me to help with anything that big before.
  -> tithe

node still hero
  The Still. They say nothing that goes in comes out. And here you are, by a fire, talking to me.
  -> tithe

node safer hero
  Maybe. Safe is what the Choir promises too, every time the collectors come.
  -> tithe

node tithe hero
  I paid the tithe like everyone. I know people who paid too much and came back Hollow. I want to know where it goes.
  -> promise

node promise commander
  Across the fire, someone laughs at a story, and the sound carries out over the dark.
  * Then we find out together. That's the whole reason we ride. -> together
    do: AddTrust $hero 8
  * Fight beside us and you'll see where it goes. -> fight
    do: AddTrust $hero 5
  * Some answers aren't worth the price. Be ready for that. -> warn
    do: AddTrust $hero 3

node together hero
  Together, then. I'll hold you to that, Commander.

node fight hero
  Fighting I can do. Point me at it.

node warn hero
  I've paid prices before. At least this time I'll know what I'm buying.
